# From "Point of Departure" (Wave VI - Odyssey, CD2-3): rotating 180 degrees
# in the energy body until face to face with the physical one, then floating
# above it to observe. Teaches its own instant-return trigger -- distinct
# from return-anchor.gws's "think one": here, the feeling of vibration and
# expansion moves you back to this exact state, not to waking.

@segment  point-of-departure
@title    Point of Departure
@levels   F12
@duration ~5m

say Calm and comfortable, floating in your energy body. Feeling lighter and lighter.
pause 6
say Slowly, think of turning over — the way you'd turn over in bed, from your back to your stomach. Either direction, whichever feels right.
pause 6
say Turn now. Notice there's no friction, no weight to it. Keep rotating, slowly, until you've turned a full hundred and eighty degrees.
pause 10
say Now, with your non-physical eyes, sense that you're face to face with your physical body. Recognise this position.
pause 8
say Calmly, think of floating upward. Up, and above your physical body.
pause 8
say Stay here, just above it, and observe. Perceive whatever there is to perceive in this new position.
hold 90
say Remember: what you've just done, you can do again. Remember the feeling of exactly where you are right now.
pause 8
say From now on, whenever you want to return to this state, all you need do is think of the feeling of vibration and expansion. You'll move calmly and confidently, right back to here.
pause 8
say The more you practice this, the easier and more effective it becomes.
pause 6
say Now, calmly, think of your physical body. Move back to it, simply by thinking of yourself, physical, and returning.
pause 8
say Move back until you feel the connection again.
pause 6
say Express gratitude now, for all you've experienced. Let it radiate through you.
pause 6
